{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:54:52.511851Z","id":"162d9491a4acf54eb8970f5ce6c4839c89bc2ab35a82966f52615927ebf6f977","body":{"detail":"Renders in target/flutter-app/home/ next to target/flutter-app/x4/launcher-*.png: same grid, sizes and tonal colours (TONES in home.js, taken from ColorScheme.fromSeed), but e.g. the money word shows a piggy-bank outline instead of Icons.savings_rounded, and Inbox/Settings are outlines. Text uses kit.css --k-font (Roboto on Android, SF in desktop Chromium), so desktop renders wrap labels slightly differently from Flutter's Roboto.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"d7d64b6afa60a5fea86c68409ef6ce2b7a5ddd2f12f2989bd53973b78ab6b717"},"summary":"The home app draws icon words, the top bar and the making states with Lucide line glyphs, where the Flutter launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart iconFor, Icons.*) uses filled Material icons; tile layout and colours match, the glyph style does not","tags":["home-app","visual","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:00:08.529522Z","id":"589bb563df256bfd2b391c12f866fbc9693ea7f4b791a8be4962f22b5f17a988","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the Clax app on Android, a long press on an app tile with no tap in the previous 5 s (for example the first touch after opening Clax, or after reading the grid for a while) shows no menu. usePress calls onHold from a setTimeout at 500 ms (line 179) or from the contextmenu event (line 187); both come while the finger is down. Touch pointerdown and contextmenu are not activation-triggering input (only touch pointerup/touchend are), and web/shell/src/caps/home.ts rejects every non-read call with no_gesture unless frameGesture() holds, whose first condition is navigator.userActivation.isActive (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:550). AppTile (line 211) drops the rejected promise silently. web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts and tests/home.test.js run over kit/fake-home.js, which never checks gestures, so nothing exercises this path; right-click (mousedown grants activation) works.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"bf170eb53b45e59c992ba1781234d270c5db1f441d793d737a321031888f2bc8"},"suggested_fix":"On touch, arm the hold at 500 ms (pressed style, optional haptic through the host) and call home.menu on that press's pointerup, which grants activation, still swallowing its click; keep the immediate call for mouse/contextmenu from a mouse. Alternatively Task 1's shell handler could accept a host-attested held press (hostArrival.pending, web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:576) for menu. Pin it with an app-mode e2e through the real shell (web/e2e/app-host.ts) holding a touch with no prior tap.","summary":"A touch long press calls home.menu while the finger is still down, before the touch grants user activation, so the shell refuses it with no_gesture and nothing happens","tags":["review","task:home-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:00:08.529648Z","id":"6b9d0c3e20fdad2311d67a22fe765868660beb92f5de9c7c3f0f8822ae081486","body":{"detail":"Every action handler calls home.<action>() and ignores the promise. The contract (web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, ClaxExtensions.Home) rejects with no_gesture, bad_request (an app deleted since the last apps event) or unavailable; the person sees a tap that does nothing and the page logs an unhandled rejection the agent's tests may count as an error.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":211},"content_hash":"de0bfc13c1c40ecfb28868722ecddb65acaa88388541edc8aadd13f3ce1153e4"},"suggested_fix":"Catch action rejections in one helper; on bad_request reload apps(), otherwise show a short toast.","summary":"Rejected home actions (open, menu, newApp, openInbox, …) are dropped silently and surface as unhandled promise rejections","tags":["review","task:home-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:00:08.529691Z","id":"e021c1f79f0e307262a9ae143a180920ae29aaaba1270688cf881e4dd13b57ab","body":{"detail":"The home app reloads only on an event without data or the Try again button shown when apps() failed with no list yet. A person used to pulling down to refresh gets nothing; if the host misses an event the grid stays stale until the app is reopened.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":363},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"123192fc9c2e8cccfd433afbf271695e2a312c06c6e2b7ab6cf143349572c03a"},"suggested_fix":"Reload all four topics on an overscroll pull at the top, or rely on Task 3's re-subscribe on resume and record that as the decision.","summary":"The launcher's pull-to-refresh (RefreshIndicator onRefresh: _load, lib/ui/launcher.dart) has no counterpart in the home app","tags":["review","task:home-2","parity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:00:08.530330Z","id":"4065cba52cf521fab9df04f723ec8fcf05b4354e0f18e93909c2f4992002bdd8","body":{"detail":"tests/home.test.js covers live updates and failures, but not an apps() answer that resolves after an apps event, which is the case the seq counter exists for.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":348},"content_hash":"989a6d5c360f709cb74c3a2f1917c87ead8afd894281c1deef5429e8bdf006f3"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test with a fake whose apps() resolves on demand: fire set({apps}) first, then resolve the stale answer, and expect the event's list to stay.","summary":"useTopic's ordering rule (an answer older than a shown event is dropped) has no test","tags":["review","task:home-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:08:47.973235Z","id":"c54ff12c6b5e708cb377855645006544f8189a1c01f593d3ec75f59745f6fdef","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:98b3721f","summary":"usePress arms the tile at 500 ms and calls onHold on that press's pointerup (activation-granting for touch). Evidence: web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts 'a touch long press arms the tile, and its release asks the app for the menu, which the shell accepts' waits for navigator.userActivation to lapse, touches via CDP with host attestations, and passes (npx playwright test e2e/home-app.spec.ts: 8 passed); with the menu called from the timer instead it fails (Received [available, apps, makes, unread, needsKey], no menu).","supersedes":"589bb563df256bfd2b391c12f866fbc9693ea7f4b791a8be4962f22b5f17a988","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:08:47.982020Z","id":"8205ef764494f33a8e80ac63b6eab7f2bf1df2e93dad5f835d726b4e82ad46d6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:98b3721f","summary":"Every action goes through useActions' act(), which catches rejections: no_gesture shows 'Tap again to …' and retries on the next tap on no other control, bad_request 'That app is no longer here', others 'Couldn't …'. Evidence: tests/home.test.js 'an action refused for want of a tap…', 'a tap on another control drops a refused action…', 'other failed actions say what went wrong' pass in the inspect view (19 passed, 0 failed).","supersedes":"6b9d0c3e20fdad2311d67a22fe765868660beb92f5de9c7c3f0f8822ae081486","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:08:47.990486Z","id":"911f1f2a4cd91cdc8a801712a3b0336acf4a6935625bb0df2260daf71887215d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:98b3721f","summary":"usePull adds pull-to-refresh from the top (a ring past 64 px reloads apps, makes, unread and key), and More > Refresh does the same with a mouse or keyboard. Evidence: tests/home.test.js 'a pull down from the top loads everything again' and 'Refresh in More loads everything again' pass in the inspect view (19 passed, 0 failed).","supersedes":"e021c1f79f0e307262a9ae143a180920ae29aaaba1270688cf881e4dd13b57ab","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:25:53.367674Z","id":"7a2b0b7a8a9f79119337b5eebad11a4b3977bcbc5b5b0e5c5bc05d23890270e0","body":{"detail":"useActions keeps a no_gesture call (home.js:428) and retries it on the next tap (home.js:444) with a fresh act() whose value nobody reads; openApp and menuOf chain their layout change (opened, star, unstar) onto the first act's promise, which resolved undefined. So an app opened through the retry keeps its New mark and gets no open counted, and Star or Unstar picked from a retried menu does nothing. A fix is for act to keep its promise pending across the retry and resolve it with the retried call's value (undefined if the kept call is dropped).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":608},"end":{"line":614},"content_hash":"a8d2dcdf0025eecddbeed729325bb59fa7130553b70481282efdfcf024e0c5fb"},"summary":"An open or a menu retried from the 'Tap again' notice is not counted and its picked item is dropped","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:29:40.697806Z","id":"126f73da421860df5c78c0316270602d24f72cbab5888ac706e8287485a6dd13","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:784edb454","summary":"useActions keeps the act() promise pending across a no_gesture retry and resolves it with the retried call's value (undefined when dropped), so openApp's opened() and menuOf's star/unstar apply. Test 'an open or a menu retried from the notice keeps its change: the open counts, the picked Star stars' in apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js fails before (waitFor gave up after 3000 ms) and passes after: pnpm exec playwright test --project=rest e2e/home-app.spec.ts -> 9 passed, harness passed 31.","supersedes":"7a2b0b7a8a9f79119337b5eebad11a4b3977bcbc5b5b0e5c5bc05d23890270e0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:34:39.476606Z","id":"ce6d27b5fab017d13bd677e20d2c23801e030448f77ddf13d7d9017c3932b1a9","body":{"detail":"openApp records opened() after home.open resolves. A cold start's HomeSnapshotCover (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart) opens the app whose recorded tile the tap fell on without the page seeing an open, so that open is not counted (bigApps in arrange.js under-ranks apps usually opened right after a cold start) and a New app opened that way stays New. Spec 2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 2 counts 'opens from the home screen'; a picture tap is one to the person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":614},"end":{"line":617},"content_hash":"66f81970c9c028ce5f05cd0a281ed6ff3acaec1903ca24b45730cbfb68384df7"},"summary":"Opens counted only through the page's own open(): a tap on the start-up picture opens the app in Clax, so it is not counted and the app keeps its New mark","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:34:39.476649Z","id":"eedc5eba5eacf7034741eda92888190500691e06d7f2779c3834e54adc94aded","body":{"detail":"normalize keeps unknown fields but coerces known ones: groups[gid].look not 'pile' becomes 'folder', an empty name becomes 'Group'; reconcile (lines 57-85) keeps in order only listed app IDs and g: keys, so an entry of a new kind a later release or an agent-changed home adds (for example a separator key) goes on the next write by this release. v is never checked, so a layout whose meaning a later release changed (v: 2) is read as v 1 and written back. system.md tells the agent 'add fields, never change the meaning of one', which these cases fall just outside; stepping back then loses them silently.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"9b4f07ad414758920f08cc4bb1861ed55a816b55943364274fedd031087eaf7c"},"suggested_fix":"Keep an unknown look and unknown order entries as they are (render the former as a folder, skip the latter), and leave a layout whose v is above 1 unwritten.","summary":"An older home app's write rewrites values it does not know: a look other than folder/pile becomes folder, a v above 1 is kept but ignored, and an order entry of an unknown kind is dropped by reconcile","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:34:39.476695Z","id":"7e99e5c37b9394039d2b71c7d1d01620b9607edb41ee4160fc439381dcc0037d","body":{"detail":"change() maps store.change's rejection (busy after 10 lease tries, a refused or failed set) to undefined, so the menu closes and the app simply does not move. start() (line 684) turns a failed use('db') into db = null, and store.js then keeps the layout in memory for the page's life: stars work until the next load, then vanish. Neither case tells the person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":586},"content_hash":"ab1298e39526dcb138fb267d8d322d84d0a2ef3d4407df0c99ae7381ea72372d"},"summary":"A Star, Unstar or open whose layout write fails says nothing: change() swallows the rejection, and a page whose use('db') failed keeps the layout in memory only","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/store.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:34:39.476731Z","id":"8beec15dc4e8c86c99cc4ad64587f7ee58969e3415fd52717975f6c74a1c2ac9","body":{"detail":"change() acquires layout/main for LEASE_MS (2000), then reads and sets without checking the lease is still held or pinning the set to the version read. If the daemon is slow (a phone waking, a busy sync), another holder acquires after 2 s, reads, writes, and this change's set then lands over it. Spec section 2 asks for writes 'pinned to the version read; on a conflict re-read, re-apply, write again'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"0c64ca54690bb2c00c7f3a3a1245d53376b668ec097b341c8eeb4ea639696562"},"summary":"The lease is 2 s and never renewed: a change whose read and set take longer can overwrite another device's change made after the lease lapsed","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/store.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:44:00.598651Z","id":"b1d1c9e36b246aeac427d8963feba9bff0055049360e8560b2a4329d96ff20ab","body":{"detail":"The page db has no conditional write: DocumentReference.set in web/contract/0.2.61/db.d.ts is a last-writer-wins full replace, DocumentSnapshot carries no version, and the shell sends every page set with lww: true (web/shell/src/caps/db.ts, case \"set\"). write() renews the lease every RENEW_MS, then renews it and re-reads just before set, so every writer using acquire on layout/main is excluded; a writer that does not (an agent's db_set, or the page's own set from another release without the lease) and lands in the window between that re-read and the set is lost. The agent's db tools pin to if_version, so their write wins only if it lands first; the page then overwrites it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"5ea2183f9a6b20e85ed7fa361526f3bf49c5b6b06b103ac7bfec59706b0bb425"},"suggested_fix":"When the page db gains a version on snapshots and an if-version set, pin the write to the version read and retry on conflict.","summary":"A layout write is not pinned to the version read: a writer that takes no lease and lands between the last re-read and set is overwritten","tags":["revisit:the page db API offers a conditional write or a document version","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:44:00.610341Z","id":"af09b84683dc9afa5cbc93c815d9d07bc46656f7488f93784e982f0f87192200","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8de7f9130","summary":"normalize keeps an unknown look (sections shows a folder), order entries of unknown kinds in place and unshown, and v of 1 or more; keepNewer (called by store.js before each write) keeps a v above 1, never lowered, and known fields of such a layout it cannot read. `npx vitest run ../apps/clax_app/home_unit` from web/: 75 passed, including the six tests under 'a layout a later release wrote' in apps/clax_app/home_unit/arrange.test.js.","supersedes":"eedc5eba5eacf7034741eda92888190500691e06d7f2779c3834e54adc94aded","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/store.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:44:00.621235Z","id":"e196a4bbe82bc9f681e1f3ce9fadedd909a2017199c8bfa67f3b426ed90d9bc4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b356b4ad4","summary":"The page db offers no conditional write, so write() renews the lease every 1 s while a change runs, then renews it and re-reads just before set, making the change again over a changed body and waiting out a lease another holder took. `npx vitest run ../apps/clax_app/home_unit` from web/: 75 passed, including 'the lease is renewed while a change runs' and 'a write landing between the read and the write is read again and the change made over it' in apps/clax_app/home_unit/store.test.js. The window left without a version pin is the waiver on apps/clax_app/home/store.js:60:81.","supersedes":"8beec15dc4e8c86c99cc4ad64587f7ee58969e3415fd52717975f6c74a1c2ac9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/motion.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:52:49.739050Z","id":"80900f7e65f10652acedbb2b66f0b409ad9b22a757c73b978a2957d127711e48","body":{"detail":"Home release 1.2.0 (apps/clax_app/home/home.js, arranger) moves tiles with these springs on requestAnimationFrame, with will-change: transform on every tile (home.css). Its tests run on a manual clock and in desktop Chromium only; no Android device was attached when 1.2.0 was packed, so no frame stats exist. To judge: with a phone attached, 'just app-phone', then 'adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo dev.empathic.clax reset', drag and toss a few tiles by hand and with 'adb shell input touchscreen draganddrop 150 600 650 600 600', then 'adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo dev.empathic.clax | grep -E \"Total frames|Janky frames|90th|95th\"'; 'adb shell screenrecord --time-limit 12 /sdcard/clax-drag.mp4' while dragging records the feel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"ff5571bfe16ed702018f213a776488f8ca1b75ef6304e56a4429f2897dc70260"},"summary":"Dragging and tossing home tiles has not been judged on a phone: frame times and feel are unmeasured","tags":["status:needs-decision","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:53:41.167238Z","id":"dc920f4845884cd45525221bd7a7b4687e32b7da24086842371a934f65ac69b5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1c00104ae","summary":"useLayout's change() calls failed() on a rejected write, which shows the notice \"Couldn't save your arrangement\", and the screen keeps the stored layout (the change shows only once written); start() mounts over a db that refuses everything when use('db') fails, so the first load already says it cannot save and a Star changes nothing. Tests in apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js: 'a Star whose write fails says so and leaves the app where it was' and 'a page whose db cannot be had says the arrangement cannot be saved, and a Star changes nothing' fail without the change (waitFor gave up) and pass with it: pnpm exec playwright test --project=rest e2e/home-app.spec.ts, 9 passed.","supersedes":"7e99e5c37b9394039d2b71c7d1d01620b9607edb41ee4160fc439381dcc0037d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:53:41.178Z","id":"481a9655afc943d06bb258bcdea59b90bfd8e30170a0a46aa2c5d4c2dee34738","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a09e65744","summary":"home.shown() now resolves {opened: id} when Clax opened app id from a tap on its start-up image (HomeHost.openReplayed, used by HomeRoute for the kept tap, in a09e65744; contract row in docs/contract.md and clax-extensions.d.ts in 106c44620), and home.js counts it with opened(), which clears New. Tests: home.test.js 'an app Clax opened from a tap on its start-up image counts as opened and loses its New mark' (fails before 106c44620, passes after; e2e/home-app.spec.ts 10 passed at 8b581423a) and test/home/home_snapshot_test.dart expecting shown to answer {'opened': notes} (failed with Actual: <null> before a09e65744; bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:home_home_snapshot_test PASSED after).","supersedes":"ce6d27b5fab017d13bd677e20d2c23801e030448f77ddf13d7d9017c3932b1a9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/drag.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:00:03.537580Z","id":"1e3048b0ead5ce5c17de45797d6f4568dccf104fc0a327b4f9716bd237d46572","body":{"detail":"Failure: a mouse drag (or a touch on a screen that sends no moves while the finger is still) that moves 20 px every 16 ms for 6 moves, then holds still 500 ms and releases, is treated as a toss at 1250 px/s and lands about 406 px (3 to 4 cells) past where it was let go. createPress.up (drag.js:49-53) passes `was.samples` without the release point; physics.js velocityOf (physics.js:109-115) measures over the 80 ms before the last sample, so time spent still before the release is never counted. Reproduced with createPress + manualClock + velocityOf in node: v = {vx: 1250, vy: 0}, toss true, tossRest x = 526 from a release at 120. home.js:552-553 then tosses. The harness tests (apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js drag(), pause: 100) send a pointermove after the pause, which hides it.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"d0903c15fb629fbd6486557262d77a11a0b0947ae4729bc5ecd076f29b550932"},"suggested_fix":"On up, push the release point at clock.now() into the samples (or drop samples older than SPEED_MS before the release time) before velocityOf; add a press test that releases after a still pause with no move in between.","summary":"A drag released after the pointer stopped still is tossed: the release speed is taken from the last pointermove samples, not up to the release time","tags":["review","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:00:03.537671Z","id":"a4b21618fe59e3b3d82b75c0cdd15be0d9da89683e5b55c68bdb9ed9ad20799b","body":{"detail":"Nothing in apps/clax_app/home/*.js listens for visibilitychange, pagehide, blur or lostpointercapture. If the page is covered or hidden mid-press (Clax routes over the WebView, the app is backgrounded, a desktop window loses the mouse) and no pointercancel reaches the document, then: the tile keeps data-held/data-dragging (pointer-events: none), `block` stays true so touchMove (home.js:617) prevents every page scroll, arranger.down (home.js:607) refuses every new press because `drag`/`active.phase` is not idle, and motion keeps the held tile so motion.moving stays true and useTiles (home.js:864) never reports tiles() again. Recovery today is a reload.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":599},"end":{"line":643},"content_hash":"65dd718a7df677d1f9005fca57c260c47b133657bdfe2cf136c464ca0e5284ca"},"suggested_fix":"On visibilitychange to hidden, pagehide, window blur and the tile's lostpointercapture, call the active press's cancel() (dragCancel/unlift).","summary":"A press or drag whose pointerup/pointercancel never arrives leaves the home screen stuck: no visibilitychange, blur or lostpointercapture recovery","tags":["review","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:00:03.537720Z","id":"bf3baf304cfc4a8ff8364768af8e92b07903a0f3e368f610593a68d77d5a9041","body":{"detail":"slotIn (home.js:437-438), dragStart's `from` (home.js:534) and dragEnd's prov (home.js:571) use st.layout, while the grid shows st.shown (the held arrangement of the previous drop, home.js:652). During a write (acquire, get, acquire, get, set in store.js:60-81; seconds when the lease is busy) a second drag re-packs from the old order, so the first-dropped tile jumps back while dragging, and the index of the second drop is taken in the old order and applied to the new one (off by one when the first app moved across it). With a cross-section first drop, `from` is wrong and the landing branch (home.js:574-581) is the wrong one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":433},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"f96b0718d4c548d24df4a9c2deda28e2b6b611918ea2fe1d562fe324c528f47b"},"suggested_fix":"Use st.shown in slotIn, dragStart and dragEnd's provisional layout.","summary":"A second drag started before the first drop's write lands is computed against the stored layout, not the shown one: the first move visibly reverts and the second can land one place off","tags":["review","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:00:03.537762Z","id":"db383a99064d8014422ce885cfdc93a149472b259622792bf0feb5edf9f3ee99","body":{"detail":"key() takes the tile's index from st.shown, but a keyboard move does not setHeld, so shown updates only when change() resolves. Two Alt+ArrowRight presses (or key repeat) within one write both compute to = i + 1 and the tile moves one cell, not two.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":625},"end":{"line":638},"content_hash":"e9f37ae09a6028f948fb4bbeafda37ceb9c013da09fa8d034f896ce4c3d51b82"},"summary":"Alt+arrows pressed again before the previous move is written are lost: each press reads the shown arrangement, which changes only after its write","tags":["review","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:00:03.537799Z","id":"d05a9a067ec10b7296beeff4f910ab9ba141eb78af28fecd0c5fb5822cacfbbc","body":{"detail":"`focus` is cleared only by a pointer down on a tile or a drag start (home.js:533, 608). A click on the page background (activeElement becomes body) followed by any render (a makes progress event, an apps event) runs relayout, which focuses the last keyboard-moved tile again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":422},"end":{"line":422},"content_hash":"ca29085e2da579d622e2e646d61f72c0888480972c83f42265e0fc0738f76f42"},"summary":"After an Alt+arrow move, any later render while nothing has focus pulls focus back to that tile","tags":["review","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:00:03.537836Z","id":"acc0c0305c9d9073d4a34ff89648a03e0ddd1c767456d9395acd847759c80a98","body":{"detail":"say() (home.js:751-755) does not drop pending.current; the document tap handler (home.js:778-785) lets a tap on .h-notice retry the kept call. Order: an open answered no_gesture keeps it and says Tap again; a layout write then fails and the notice reads Couldn't save your arrangement; tapping that notice opens the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":751},"end":{"line":755},"content_hash":"c578e2e31ce0047d79697b4ff576a0d5e372b0ebe0374433e2959bfae66dfae4"},"summary":"\"Couldn't save your arrangement\" replaces a \"Tap again to …\" notice but keeps its call: a tap on the save-failure notice then retries the kept open or menu","tags":["review","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/drag.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:02:58.900508Z","id":"d5fbcefa7d8bdf504477d949403c66cf58275ccb70d3eb6b649478aae51045bc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:da9fd07e8","summary":"Fixed: up() in apps/clax_app/home/drag.js now ends a drag with the release point (clock time) as the newest sample, and velocityOf in apps/clax_app/home/physics.js takes the speed over the SPEED_MS up to it. apps/clax_app/home_unit/drag.test.js 'a drag held still 500 ms before the release is not tossed' (six 20 px moves 16 ms apart, 500 ms still, release) gives {vx: 0, vy: 0}, was 1250 px/s; 'a drag released while moving keeps its speed' gives 1250 px/s. Evidence: `npx vitest run ../apps/clax_app/home_unit` from web/: 8 files, 79 tests passed; `bazelisk test //web:unit //web:lint`: 2 tests pass.","supersedes":"1e3048b0ead5ce5c17de45797d6f4568dccf104fc0a327b4f9716bd237d46572","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:06:21.726848Z","id":"8b57f59069e110582f68c9c574a6d8306e33eefc6facf5fb060fb32f58dbd241","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c92d59c32","summary":"say() now drops the kept call before showing its notice. Harness test \"the save-failure notice drops the kept call it replaces: a tap on it opens nothing\" (apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js) fails without the change (opens 2) and passes with it: web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts \"its tests in the inspect view\" 1 passed.","supersedes":"acc0c0305c9d9073d4a34ff89648a03e0ddd1c767456d9395acd847759c80a98","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:06:21.738152Z","id":"8322c2cd33c711fdf635120eb6fbf403071f0e196d35d7c6ca41190c8dc458a1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:899baa276","summary":"key() shows its move at once (st.shown and setHeld), so a second press moves on from it. Harness test \"Alt+arrows pressed again before the first move is written both count\" fails without the change and passes with it (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts \"its tests in the inspect view\": 1 passed).","supersedes":"db383a99064d8014422ce885cfdc93a149472b259622792bf0feb5edf9f3ee99","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:06:21.749289Z","id":"17e88e2dd4e9c78c4c1e1bac4f6401995f9007940d4404839af3997b9cbc53c5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b733463ff","summary":"A pointerdown or focusin anywhere but the moved tile clears `focus` (arranger.elsewhere). Harness test \"after an Alt+arrow move, a press elsewhere keeps a later render from focusing the tile\" fails without the change (activeElement app-run) and passes with it.","supersedes":"d05a9a067ec10b7296beeff4f910ab9ba141eb78af28fecd0c5fb5822cacfbbc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:06:21.760457Z","id":"b9f8210bdec3cfca21508cbb06827aa22ff431442a634b5a0dfc24a92fc898ac","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5dc734b83","summary":"slotIn, retarget, dragStart's from and dragEnd's prov read st.shown. Harness tests \"a second drag before the first drop is written starts from the arrangement shown\" and \"a drop into Starred dragged again before it is written lands in Starred\" fail without the change and pass with it.","supersedes":"bf3baf304cfc4a8ff8364768af8e92b07903a0f3e368f610593a68d77d5a9041","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T04:06:21.772076Z","id":"323b8ffa6cd469da9db3488a6e540f333c76aec130329ceb2770f6083673bada","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ddcf0fefd","summary":"visibilitychange (hidden), pagehide, window blur and lostpointercapture call arranger.abandon(): the press is cancelled and motion.rest() puts every tile in place and settles, so tiles() reports again. Harness tests \"a drag whose release never comes ends when the page loses focus, and the tiles are reported again\" and \"a held press ends when the page is hidden or the pointer is lost\" fail without the change and pass with it; vitest home_unit/motion.test.js \"rest puts every tile in place...\" passes.","supersedes":"a4b21618fe59e3b3d82b75c0cdd15be0d9da89683e5b55c68bdb9ed9ad20799b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T05:29:39.746681Z","id":"2d80df2a8f02dca7bc4a4a8c4269659f2e29fe5c7c94d9586f69e49bfccee1b0","body":{"detail":"With an immediate reorder, approaching another app's centre always passes through its slot's outer region first, which moves that app aside before the pointer reaches its 24 px centre zone (grid.js centreUnder), so the app can never be grouped with. track() (home.js:581) therefore commits a new slot only after the pointer rests REORDER_MS in it, and a pointer on a centre cancels the pending move. Neighbours now make room 120 ms later than in 1.2.0. The plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-17-launcher-arrange.md Task 9 step 3.2) did not name this delay.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":389},"end":{"line":393},"content_hash":"6038c0a3f5cd1c42673f8a2faa5bf7a138d96b85e9e0693e94d2c7d7d263cf5a"},"summary":"Reorder at once as the pointer crosses into a new slot (release 1.2.0's rule), instead of after REORDER_MS (120 ms) at rest","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a phone judgment of dragging finds the 120 ms delay before neighbours move noticeable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T05:29:39.746775Z","id":"ae85a27d1e688fc9d3c5b69de0c8b93fa91f5254c0fa661b1bae4ba971e8e07a","body":{"detail":"The main grid moves a focused tile with Alt+arrows (arranger.key). Inside an open folder the same keys do nothing, so a keyboard-only person cannot reorder a group's apps; they can still Remove from group from the menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1067},"end":{"line":1067},"content_hash":"f374e11880548aa884469c846a2e2ab3e47606c34ceff7e379675627e5e144b0"},"summary":"Alt+arrows do nothing on a tile inside an open folder: folderArranger's key() is empty, so the folder's order changes only by dragging","tags":["a11y","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T13:44:53.712589Z","id":"e06c5ee37e0374ff5470dd1a9b0687fd71192e8cc274cf516a3c128c41652510","body":{"detail":"fanHandlersFor gives the fan's tiles a press whose dragStart, dragMove and dragEnd do nothing; the open folder (folderArranger) lets an app be dragged to reorder or out past its edge. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 5 asks only that the pile fan out and gather, so this is a gap against the folder, not the spec.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":731},"end":{"line":757},"content_hash":"5d46ee30532b664c28e23c58c56328cfdd625d61e06eeb24a8871f63dfd3255a"},"summary":"An app in a fanned pile's row cannot be dragged: a hold then a move does nothing, so it leaves the pile only by Remove from group in its menu, and reorders only by Alt+Left/Right","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T13:44:53.712929Z","id":"9ed0af2619ebb5b20dd43d9a6f94173738b4748bfa6f12859cbdd99f3feee30a","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":780},"end":{"line":786},"content_hash":"6074fadf94cf5fb5e2883f255e5c74a5aaf949e66042544d95ec9c903eeeb9ef"},"summary":"A drag that starts while a pile is fanned out gathers it at once, with no motion (gatherNow): slotIn and the toss's slots pack All apps without the fan's row, so a drop under an open fan would land a row off","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T13:49:52.184384Z","id":"803d3c174916b07770993411eaf822aa4ab04db2eda027de17bc16bb56ccdcd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a20642281","summary":"Fixed: folderArranger's key() moves the focused app one place left or right, or a row up or down, within the group (apps/clax_app/home/home.js). Evidence: the harness test 'Alt+arrows move a focused app within an open folder, and two presses before the write both count' in apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js passes: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app reports 12 passed, the harness 66 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"ae85a27d1e688fc9d3c5b69de0c8b93fa91f5254c0fa661b1bae4ba971e8e07a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:02:09.744352Z","id":"19dc9b45f320b702a3a2459bd3eeffd6fb5f7cb3041729fd7ea515c34a0c7dd2","body":{"detail":"track() returns before any reorder while hoverAt finds a centre within 24 px (grid.js centreUnder), so a person who lays the dragged icon over the tile whose place they want (the pointer then sits on that tile's centre) sees nothing move and, at HOVER_MS (600 ms), the outline; a release then makes a folder. setHover marks a group's key ready at once (no HOVER_MS), and dragEnd (home.js:835) checks hover before the toss, so a release while the pointer crosses a folder's or pile's centre, a fast flick included, adds the app to that group. The plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-17-launcher-arrange.md Task 9 step 3.2) starts the 600 ms timer for an app or a group target. Not judged on a phone; see also 2d80df2a on REORDER_MS.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":633},"end":{"line":693},"content_hash":"17fdc90f3df917e3efa390a2c0a8340d7dcbfa67c434ff13743d2546f200ec38"},"suggested_fix":"Give a group target the same HOVER_MS as an app, skip groupDrop when the release is a toss (velocityOf over TOSS_MIN), and consider letting the target make room once the pointer rests on its centre past HOVER_MS without a release.","summary":"A reorder that ends on a tile's centre can group by accident: on an app's centre the neighbours never make room, and on a group's centre the app goes in at once, tossed or not","tags":["review","home","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:02:09.744565Z","id":"e468b5cf2afcd2695344b2da2b862e307d1baf4a3554f5884fe27fbe692e7e50","body":{"detail":"hoverAt (apps/clax_app/home/home.js:610) looks for centres in Starred too, and makeGroup puts a group whose target is not in order last in All apps (at = -1). The person drops in Starred, sees the starred app vanish with the dragged one, and finds the folder only by scrolling to the end of All apps. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 5 does not say where such a group goes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":232},"end":{"line":251},"content_hash":"d31d1da605757c62478a45d651776ff0744af2426d47c9654f4296beafacd13c"},"suggested_fix":"Either do not hover-group over Starred apps (hoverAt over 'all' only), or put the group first in All apps so it shows right under Starred.","summary":"Dropping an app on a starred app makes the folder at the end of All apps: both apps leave Starred and the new folder can land off screen","tags":["review","home","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:02:09.744795Z","id":"64941f6b44713026ddf09d971fa8e7cf4b61660d66315299230ca8123b6f1b5c","body":{"detail":"openGroup and fanGroup push a #group entry so back closes them (folderNav); showGroupMenu only sets state. With the menu open, Android back finds no page history, so Clax handles it as back from the home screen, and the menu is still open when the page shows again. Escape and the scrim close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1498},"end":{"line":1517},"content_hash":"65f1639d5f26a5c7f441a59463f567a187c021d383c0ecb6a079979c3ce0e724"},"suggested_fix":"Close the group menu on popstate, or push the same #group entry when it opens.","summary":"System back does not close the group's own menu: it has no history entry, unlike the folder and the fan","tags":["review","home","navigation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:15:38.443702Z","id":"113dbb3bc867a1bf4ebc19da3af189e12b9e5aed2c51bb45f65ea3e7951d165c","body":{"detail":"bigApps (arrange.js) ranks by opens in the last 14 days (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 6); {n, last} alone cannot say how many opens fell in a window. Day counts stay bounded (at most 14 keys per app) and readable by every release from 1.1.0, which writes them. A list of timestamps grows with use; a decaying score cannot answer a fixed window.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"3bcc1f6b4687980665ab08d415d1efd7656cab4618aa3bce4775bd4491242aed"},"summary":"Each opens entry keeps per-day counts (days: {\"YYYY-MM-DD\": n}, UTC days, the last OPEN_DAYS kept) beside {n, last}, instead of a list of open times or a decaying score","tags":["revisit:the big-tile rule changes from a 14-day window to a longer window or a decaying score","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:15:38.443862Z","id":"601a9061c309cc0ad3e6836f67e39103843f97f552576761db6e4096fc5b74ab","body":{"detail":"placement moves the rows after bandEnd down one and fanRowOf puts the fan there, so the fan never crosses a big tile; the 1×1 tiles in the band's second row then sit between the pile and its fan (test: 'a pile fanned out beside a big tile opens its row under the big tile's rows, over nothing' in apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js). Not taken: the fan right under the pile's row with the big tile pushed down and split across it, or re-packing All apps with the big tile moved past the fan.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"4b309540a828de0fc248ef9bef26de3a41fedf0812415d275174beff0d2d69a2"},"summary":"A pile fanned out beside a 2×2 tile opens its row under the band of rows the 2×2 covers (bandEnd), not directly under the pile's own row","tags":["revisit:a pile next to a big tile reads as detached from its fanned row on a phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T14:15:38.443946Z","id":"6c496a02d5b2cf139b8db3c0a5ce2b7cab6c812012961e518c392c8b4d3a01fa","body":{"detail":"slotIn takes the dragged entry's span from bigApps(st.shown), where a starred app is never big. Once the provisional move (drag.prov) puts it in All apps, placement may give it a 2×2, and the slot chosen by the pointer was computed for a 1×1 packed in the same place. track() recomputes on every move, so the shown slot converges, but the first commit after crossing into All apps can be a cell off. No test drags a starred app with enough opens to grow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":615},"end":{"line":642},"content_hash":"ec859e5def8da74285c4eb2e6af3b10d29762a5f32fd7ebc0403311cd4be4e94"},"summary":"Dragging a starred app into All apps sizes its slot as a 1×1 even when it would grow there, so the drop can land a cell off from where the 2×2 shows","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:54:20.545596Z","id":"eababe2045111ea27f11c11f4c175c5936921613c18a35d39620e13100eabf1b","body":{"detail":"Renders in target/flutter-app/home/ next to target/flutter-app/x4/launcher-*.png: same grid, sizes and tonal colours (TONES in home.js, taken from ColorScheme.fromSeed), but e.g. the money word shows a piggy-bank outline instead of Icons.savings_rounded, and Inbox/Settings are outlines. Text uses kit.css --k-font (Roboto on Android, SF in desktop Chromium), so desktop renders wrap labels slightly differently from Flutter's Roboto.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":65},"content_hash":"30116d817e91a1d8e5c9e98340391f27962d28d530d5787005440f41c545c525"},"summary":"The home app draws icon words, the top bar and the making states with Lucide line glyphs, where the Flutter launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart iconFor, Icons.*) uses filled Material icons; tile layout and colours match, the glyph style does not","supersedes":"162d9491a4acf54eb8970f5ce6c4839c89bc2ab35a82966f52615927ebf6f977","tags":["home-app","visual","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:54:20.556948Z","id":"0679ba2061c2174daef9a9b7fe20e8f92d069056cd703c3852509362caeaa01e","body":{"detail":"tests/home.test.js covers live updates and failures, but not an apps() answer that resolves after an apps event, which is the case the seq counter exists for.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1686},"end":{"line":1716},"content_hash":"55a3afe43614c659a2b01008afbce05a44504784f8d68ff39945da3e5c474929"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test with a fake whose apps() resolves on demand: fire set({apps}) first, then resolve the stale answer, and expect the event's list to stay.","summary":"useTopic's ordering rule (an answer older than a shown event is dropped) has no test","supersedes":"4065cba52cf521fab9df04f723ec8fcf05b4354e0f18e93909c2f4992002bdd8","tags":["review","task:home-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:54:20.568015Z","id":"5ebc57858eba942228e2634b68f7a94149705b0a2569373baa59ff27fe45c0f7","body":{"detail":"placement moves the rows after bandEnd down one and fanRowOf puts the fan there, so the fan never crosses a big tile; the 1×1 tiles in the band's second row then sit between the pile and its fan (test: 'a pile fanned out beside a big tile opens its row under the big tile's rows, over nothing' in apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js). Not taken: the fan right under the pile's row with the big tile pushed down and split across it, or re-packing All apps with the big tile moved past the fan.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":385},"content_hash":"4b309540a828de0fc248ef9bef26de3a41fedf0812415d275174beff0d2d69a2"},"summary":"A pile fanned out beside a 2×2 tile opens its row under the band of rows the 2×2 covers (bandEnd), not directly under the pile's own row","supersedes":"601a9061c309cc0ad3e6836f67e39103843f97f552576761db6e4096fc5b74ab","tags":["revisit:a pile next to a big tile reads as detached from its fanned row on a phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:54:20.578863Z","id":"2371ae9608e20c14a71883297682ee821cb0d9b9d2e694a1db54fb187a91d841","body":{"detail":"The neighbours make room only after the pointer rests REORDER_MS in a new slot, on a tile's centre as anywhere (home.js track). The delay first let a pointer reach an app's 24 px centre zone before that app moved aside; grouping now needs a 600 ms rest within that zone moving at most 8 px, and then brings the hovered tile back under the pointer (home.js followHover), so the delay now only keeps quick passes from shuffling tiles. Neighbours make room 120 ms later than in release 1.2.0. The plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-17-launcher-arrange.md Task 9 step 3.2) did not name this delay.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":500},"end":{"line":502},"content_hash":"845f7a975ceb513d7fb666138ba61d56bd145f50e7b4ff8639f962ea57d48c17"},"summary":"Reorder at once as the pointer crosses into a new slot (release 1.2.0's rule), instead of after REORDER_MS (120 ms) at rest","supersedes":"2d80df2a8f02dca7bc4a4a8c4269659f2e29fe5c7c94d9586f69e49bfccee1b0","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a phone judgment of dragging finds the 120 ms delay before neighbours move noticeable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/motion.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:54:20.589673Z","id":"99ef2afb95ffde8e1ac1aa295bd7febc6922d52bd6c46b7304facb43d73c03a0","body":{"detail":"Home release 1.2.0 (apps/clax_app/home/home.js, arranger) moves tiles with these springs on requestAnimationFrame, with will-change: transform on every tile (home.css). Its tests run on a manual clock and in desktop Chromium only; no Android device was attached when 1.2.0 was packed, so no frame stats exist. To judge: with a phone attached, 'just app-phone', then 'adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo dev.empathic.clax reset', drag and toss a few tiles by hand and with 'adb shell input touchscreen draganddrop 150 600 650 600 600', then 'adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo dev.empathic.clax | grep -E \"Total frames|Janky frames|90th|95th\"'; 'adb shell screenrecord --time-limit 12 /sdcard/clax-drag.mp4' while dragging records the feel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"0586bb66a8289025e7f7136038f0dd1dc5fc2b7716ffb1559656525450fb6ca8"},"summary":"Dragging and tossing home tiles has not been judged on a phone: frame times and feel are unmeasured","supersedes":"80900f7e65f10652acedbb2b66f0b409ad9b22a757c73b978a2957d127711e48","tags":["status:needs-decision","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:55:36.933503Z","id":"86a67b9c67d25b58fe221c88ec4cadbdeec5d3370c40ed80cf29e8b3bee5ce79","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4afe57854","summary":"Fixed: the neighbours make room on a tile's centre too, a hover readies only after the pointer stays within 24 px of the centre, moving at most 8 px, for 600 ms (apps and groups alike), and dragEnd checks the toss first. Tests in apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js \"resting on an app's centre makes room there…\", \"a pointer that keeps moving about an app's centre never groups\", \"a group is outlined only after a 600 ms rest…\", \"a toss or a fast move over a group never adds to it…\" failed on the parent commit and pass: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app: tests/home.test.js 87 passed, 0 failed (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts)","supersedes":"19dc9b45f320b702a3a2459bd3eeffd6fb5f7cb3041729fd7ea515c34a0c7dd2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:55:36.944829Z","id":"b4cf35533033f85cbefa67cd6796aa02b3a951da8190d9cdf0f33914121e5311","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9711b42f4","summary":"Fixed: groups cannot be starred (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md, decisions), so makeGroup puts a folder made on a starred app first in All apps and the page scrolls it into view. home_unit/arrange.test.js \"a starred target leaves Starred for the new group, first in All apps…\" (bazelisk test //web:unit PASSED) and home.test.js \"an app held over a starred app makes the folder first in All apps, scrolled into view\" failed before and pass: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app: tests/home.test.js 87 passed, 0 failed (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts)","supersedes":"e468b5cf2afcd2695344b2da2b862e307d1baf4a3554f5884fe27fbe692e7e50","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:55:36.955882Z","id":"d54fe8f2d7e13702826ea35005bf940a8a524b0ce414fcf8000f71c02bddb715","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7db49c962","summary":"Fixed: the group menu takes a #menu history entry; back closes it, and over a fanned pile closes only the menu. home.test.js \"back closes the group's own menu, and only it; Escape leaves its history entry too\" failed before (history.state undefined) and passes: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app: tests/home.test.js 87 passed, 0 failed (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts)","supersedes":"64941f6b44713026ddf09d971fa8e7cf4b61660d66315299230ca8123b6f1b5c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:55:36.966741Z","id":"26b5dfce287269572ff963a7632b4bcde4f340f3cc829fb944f30bb5eced70d4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d13df34bd","summary":"Fixed: a fanned pile's app drags along its row (moveInGroup) or out into the grid, leaving the group. home.test.js \"an app dragged along a fanned pile's row reorders the group…\" and \"an app dragged out of a fanned pile's row into the grid leaves the group there\" failed before and pass: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app: tests/home.test.js 87 passed, 0 failed (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts)","supersedes":"e06c5ee37e0374ff5470dd1a9b0687fd71192e8cc274cf516a3c128c41652510","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:55:36.977667Z","id":"4a89724883577fb90624616580b4a998d7834b430d823152106f02f8351e3057","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d13df34bd","summary":"Fixed: a drag gathers a fanned pile only when the pile itself is dragged; slotIn counts the fan's row as placement draws it. home.test.js \"a drag while a pile is fanned keeps it fanned and drops where the tiles show, past the fan's row\" failed before and passes: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app: tests/home.test.js 87 passed, 0 failed (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts)","supersedes":"9ed0af2619ebb5b20dd43d9a6f94173738b4748bfa6f12859cbdd99f3feee30a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T15:55:36.988705Z","id":"578020f49513b2979146832afaa14b928ea3ccf433f3a42a038554801c03eb3b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0a149ee9c","summary":"Fixed: slotIn sizes All apps' entries with bigApps of the arrangement that has the dragged entry in All apps. home.test.js \"a starred app dragged into All apps, where it grows, takes the slot its 2×2 shows at\" failed before (Expected: 4 to be 3) and passes: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app: tests/home.test.js 87 passed, 0 failed (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts)","supersedes":"6c496a02d5b2cf139b8db3c0a5ce2b7cab6c812012961e518c392c8b4d3a01fa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:02:13.949110Z","id":"7a181ad20f7696b2f2a85453c2d92dae1efbc41c6b8443dbe11a250ef2ee5ee2","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home screen short enough not to scroll (scrollY stays 0), a pile of more apps than columns fanned out (.h-fan, overflow-x: auto, home.css:406-409), and a sideways swipe on its row whose first touchmove has clientY one pixel or more below the touchstart: usePullSearch's window touchmove (passive: false) calls preventDefault on that first move (dy > 0, no check of dx or of the touch's target), so the browser cancels native scrolling for the whole touch sequence; the row does not scroll and the search ghost slides in instead. The same holds for any horizontally scrolling element under the touch. Only data-held tiles and an open .h-folder are exempt (home.js:1805-1812).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1809},"end":{"line":1817},"content_hash":"9e43990ca48855721dda538272b89eaf723c1d5188df1ae5eb83f1579ca667e7"},"suggested_fix":"Decide the gesture's axis on the first move past a few px (ignore the pull when |dx| > dy), and leave touches that start inside .h-fan (or any element scrolled horizontally) to the browser.","summary":"The pull to search takes every touch that starts with the page at the top and first moves down, so a fanned pile's row cannot be swiped sideways when the finger drifts down","tags":["review","touch","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:02:13.949471Z","id":"ac4fe30955311c92b3adc4f35cd45348c226816a9bb4cdc6bc3b709056683aa8","body":{"detail":"With search open and its field empty the grid shows (home.js:2197-2208), so a group's menu can open over it: history is base, #search, #menu. Picking Rename runs closeGroupMenu (nav.leave('menu') starts a history.back()), then openGroup -> closeSearch -> nav.leave('search'), which skips its own back because nav.back is already set (home.js:1985-1990); nav.enter('group') then pushes #group when the menu's back lands on #search. History ends base, #search, #group with search closed: back closes the folder and the next back does nothing visible. Not covered by tests/home.test.js.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2056},"end":{"line":2063},"content_hash":"2c821a8eb3d401a6e003af84c7728f1b6e425fc6b94e17c3b51a229e3f196ed2"},"suggested_fix":"Let nav.leave(kind) queue its back when one is in flight (count pending backs), or have the popstate handler pop a stale kind whose closer already ran before pushing `push`.","summary":"Rename from a group's menu opened while search is open with an empty field leaves a dead #search history entry under the folder","tags":["review","history","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:02:13.949583Z","id":"6d1187ea5a9327e740a605c3f771326fc4a4ccca52ae722b27dea877551bc1ae","body":{"detail":"hoverAt and centreUnder (grid.js:62-67) use cellBox's centre with CENTRE_PX = 24. A 1x1 cell is 116 px tall with its 60 px icon at 8-68 px, so the hover centre (58 px) is 20 px below the icon's centre. A 2x2 cell is 240 px tall with its 120 px icon at 8-128 px (aligned to the first row since 4506018da), so the hover centre (120 px) is 52 px below the icon's centre (68 px): a person holding a dragged app over the middle of a big app's icon gets no outline and no group; only the band from the icon's lower quarter to just under it groups.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":716},"end":{"line":733},"content_hash":"354bb5ed2ed91b24a201fafc6cc941ae9873efcdbf10ccd54774d545ee5d2120"},"suggested_fix":"Hover on the target's .h-icon centre (from its drawn rect, or cellBox plus the icon's offset) rather than the cell's.","summary":"Grouping aims at the cell's centre, not the icon's: on a big tile the pointer on its icon's centre never groups","tags":["review","drag","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:02:13.949663Z","id":"458a13aeb0bc6deeee977704fbcec9649187490b23a986fae7e281e7e0c1d802","body":{"detail":"dragEnd sets el.style.visibility = 'hidden' on the fan tile (p:<id>) and a `landing` for a:<id>, expecting the next render to drop the fan tile. When st.change rejects (UNSAVED_TEXT: db unavailable, home.js start() with home but no db, or a refused write) the layout keeps the app in its group, Preact keeps the same keyed fan element, and nothing clears visibility: the app is invisible in the fan until the pile is gathered and fanned again; the unused `landing` is applied to a later relayout of a:<id>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1001},"end":{"line":1012},"content_hash":"d8247734e092db0201e5d122ba6b649929fee3e0729162988f02f933fef8a888"},"suggested_fix":"Clear the fan tile's visibility and `landing` when st.change resolves undefined (or always after setHeld(null)).","summary":"An app dragged out of a fanned pile stays hidden in the row when the write fails","tags":["review","drag","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:02:13.950851Z","id":"6c9c37437c802c7c2e7b147f27757f829b92f5eabedda5f80125f5be9736835f","body":{"detail":"bigApps ranks by 14-day count, then by `last`. With apps A and B both at 5 opens in third place, opening either makes it the later `last` and so the big one: the grid reflows each time the person comes back, which reads as tiles flickering between 2x2 and 1x1. The day window also drops a count at 00:00 UTC, so a tile can shrink mid-session at a local time unrelated to use. The rule follows docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 6, which is silent on ties.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"a43627326253a930ce9d16bdf3468be391ae9f19f8e87bdc7733776967c2d9bc"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the current big apps unless a challenger passes them by a margin (or ties keep the incumbent), and judge the window by local day.","summary":"Big tiles have no hysteresis: apps tied at the third place swap 2x2 cells on every open, and an app at exactly BIG_MIN shrinks at a UTC midnight","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.654705Z","id":"5f7abe89067c7dd4866a549c3e682e41a9a307fa656756920811e01e9c4bfdd0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d4f84f15","summary":"usePullSearch (home.js:1781-1859) decides on the first 6 px (PULL_DECIDE_PX): a pull only when dy > |dx|, from scrollY 0, outside an element scrolled sideways (inSidewaysScroll); preventDefault only after that. Test \"a sideways swipe on a fanned pile's row is the row's, however it drifts down; a pull is taken only once it is mostly down\" (tests/home.test.js) failed before the change ([true,true,true] for the row's touchmoves) and passes: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app --runs_per_test=6 -> 14 passed in each run.","supersedes":"7a181ad20f7696b2f2a85453c2d92dae1efbc41c6b8443dbe11a250ef2ee5ee2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.696442Z","id":"314827ef557724f2ee3bc539231202360f9c427bf62fe906ab899f9daa56cbf4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:115c0a394","summary":"nav (home.js:1976-2037) keeps each entry's kinds under it in its state and counts backs: a leave while a back is on its way adds its own (history.go once that lands), so Rename from a menu over search leaves base, #group. web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts \"Rename from a group's menu opened over search leaves one entry, which one back pops\" (page.goBack) failed before (hash #search after one back) and passes: //web:e2e_rest --grep=home-app, 14 passed, three runs.","supersedes":"ac4fe30955311c92b3adc4f35cd45348c226816a9bb4cdc6bc3b709056683aa8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.737532Z","id":"36c5e5bc47527031089d2515fc43b02a498d3d18eb154f39b05936867c07cb2f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9d8406924","summary":"grid.js iconCentre (8 px down the cell, 60 px icon, 120 on a 2x2) is what centreUnder and hoverAt now measure from. home_unit/grid.test.js \"centreUnder aims at the icon's centre...\" and tests/home.test.js \"a big tile drags ... an app held on its icon's centre groups with it\" (aimed at the .h-face centre) failed before and pass: //web:unit PASSED; //web:e2e_rest --grep=home-app 14 passed, three runs.","supersedes":"6d1187ea5a9327e740a605c3f771326fc4a4ccca52ae722b27dea877551bc1ae","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.778447Z","id":"70c8eeccea4ae0708e2edc90d8b3cdf4e0984dd585960b050d067b073f57262c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6e93ccdda","summary":"Does not happen: dragEnd's st.setHeld(d.prov) renders the arrangement with the app out of the group before the write's failure lands (store.change is always async, Preact renders on a microtask), so the hidden p:<id> tile leaves the row and the a:<id> tile there consumes `landing`; on the failure the row draws the app as a new, visible element. Test \"an app dragged out of a fanned pile whose write fails shows in the row again\" (tests/home.test.js) checks the element is new and visible; it passed with no change to home.js (//web:e2e_rest --grep=home-app, 14 passed, three runs).","supersedes":"458a13aeb0bc6deeee977704fbcec9649187490b23a986fae7e281e7e0c1d802","tags":["reason:invalid","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.820460Z","id":"15dd68df371c574baa5e1d5a1c5dcc0dc30b5c3eeea4366cf1059e9d1c6207b8","body":{"detail":"The neighbours make room only after the pointer rests REORDER_MS in a new slot, on a tile's centre as anywhere (home.js track). The delay first let a pointer reach an app's 24 px centre zone before that app moved aside; grouping now needs a 600 ms rest within that zone moving at most 8 px, and then brings the hovered tile back under the pointer (home.js followHover), so the delay now only keeps quick passes from shuffling tiles. Neighbours make room 120 ms later than in release 1.2.0. The plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-17-launcher-arrange.md Task 9 step 3.2) did not name this delay.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":501},"end":{"line":503},"content_hash":"845f7a975ceb513d7fb666138ba61d56bd145f50e7b4ff8639f962ea57d48c17"},"summary":"Reorder at once as the pointer crosses into a new slot (release 1.2.0's rule), instead of after REORDER_MS (120 ms) at rest","supersedes":"2371ae9608e20c14a71883297682ee821cb0d9b9d2e694a1db54fb187a91d841","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a phone judgment of dragging finds the 120 ms delay before neighbours move noticeable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.862045Z","id":"6b1e69cfbf07f0e6b11e1cbe967de9590e83e00fd93640bba81f5bc6cc068d2b","body":{"detail":"bigApps (arrange.js) ranks by opens in the last 14 days (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 6); {n, last} alone cannot say how many opens fell in a window. Day counts stay bounded (at most 14 keys per app) and readable by every release from 1.1.0, which writes them. A list of timestamps grows with use; a decaying score cannot answer a fixed window.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"3bcc1f6b4687980665ab08d415d1efd7656cab4618aa3bce4775bd4491242aed"},"summary":"Each opens entry keeps per-day counts (days: {\"YYYY-MM-DD\": n}, UTC days, the last OPEN_DAYS kept) beside {n, last}, instead of a list of open times or a decaying score","supersedes":"113dbb3bc867a1bf4ebc19da3af189e12b9e5aed2c51bb45f65ea3e7951d165c","tags":["revisit:the big-tile rule changes from a 14-day window to a longer window or a decaying score","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:55.905025Z","id":"b0a0d9e6a353caa9892bf6cd92f0d47b805f85ac40c34ae36b1ddb17f53ec80e","body":{"detail":"bigApps ranks by 14-day count, then by `last`. With apps A and B both at 5 opens in third place, opening either makes it the later `last` and so the big one: the grid reflows each time the person comes back, which reads as tiles flickering between 2x2 and 1x1. The day window also drops a count at 00:00 UTC, so a tile can shrink mid-session at a local time unrelated to use. The rule follows docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-launcher-arrange-design.md section 6, which is silent on ties.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":239},"content_hash":"680cab7e2223de1e407421a1a4e1e3204118cf44c43aebeebdd3f16b947296c6"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the current big apps unless a challenger passes them by a margin (or ties keep the incumbent), and judge the window by local day.","summary":"Big tiles have no hysteresis: apps tied at the third place swap 2x2 cells on every open, and an app at exactly BIG_MIN shrinks at a UTC midnight","supersedes":"6c9c37437c802c7c2e7b147f27757f829b92f5eabedda5f80125f5be9736835f","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/arrange.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T16:45:06.716628Z","id":"4ed67d83dd17773ce5da8dc9f862637a806ddbbd68c2f190ee03c6ef3a1330a7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b0a0d9e6a353caa9892bf6cd92f0d47b805f85ac40c34ae36b1ddb17f53ec80e","summary":"Rule now in arrange.js bigApps/keepBig (84effeb7c), for the owner to confirm or change: each layout write stores the apps on 2x2 tiles as `big` (home.js useLayout change ranks from the set shown before the change, so a layout without `big` starts from what it showed). In bigApps an app in `big` scores its 14-day opens + BIG_KEEP - 0.5 (BIG_KEEP = 2): it wins a tie at the boundary, keeps its tile down to BIG_MIN - 1 = 4 opens (shrinks at 3) and against an app with 1 open more, and gives way to one with 2 or more. Other ties still go to the later open, then the ID. The window is still UTC days; an app at 5 that loses one open at 00:00 UTC keeps its tile, one that loses two shrinks. Tests: home_unit/arrange.test.js bigApps (ties, margin, floor, keepBig) and tests/home.test.js 'opening an app that ties the third big tile leaves the big tiles as they are'. Not chosen: local-day windows; passing the previous set as an argument instead of storing it (a reload or another device would lose it).","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:01:28.374441Z","id":"e3a4062495cac85d634909c6cecf5ff66136f80ddc92de0836b7f7361d79c850","body":{"detail":"The lift shadow alias (home.css:25) is var(--elev-3); the hand-kept dark value it replaced added a 1 px ring (0 0 0 1px rgba(226,226,233,.22)). Spec §1.6 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md) pairs dark elevation with a 1 px border-hover outline, which the elev tokens in home/tokens.css do not include; the held and dragging tile faces (home.css:223) need that outline in dark.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"107a2dd896f2fbb5970fd28ea228519752464534ea05d62840d4951feeb71fad"},"summary":"In dark mode a held or dragged tile casts only the elev-3 shadow, with no outline, so the lift barely shows on bg #141413","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.981969Z","id":"e7be1a689221fdfa64dba1e68365eaaee8a71cdafacf69ed517cf28540bf633e","body":{"detail":"design/tokens.json gives overlay and hover the same dark value (§1.2 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md), and the alias layer maps --h-state to hover and --h-menu-bg to overlay, so .h-menu-item:hover/:active paints the same colour as the menu. Light is visible (#f2f2ef on #ffffff).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"c6c4010c7ac22d360322271df60c53144589315cba97ee2f90ccc843bdb00391"},"suggested_fix":"A hover on overlay one step lighter (border-hover #3a3a36, or a translucent fg), and the same for any Flutter surface drawn on overlay with hoverColor.","summary":"In dark mode a home menu item shows no hover or press: --h-state (hover #2a2a27) on --h-menu-bg (overlay #2a2a27)","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.982373Z","id":"ef32771d27ca50788a1d3d32df30bb1ff9ea0729bb46ee5297132b64cef292f4","body":{"detail":"Lines 106, 156, 217, 244, 250, 341, 346 and 376 run in the same Android WebView the kit guards against (record 2f7a336048). Without color-mix the text-button hover, the scrim at 156, the FAB press, the drop zone's dashed border and fill, the folder-out panel and the search field fill all compute to unset. sync-tokens.py's guard check reads kit.css only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":376},"content_hash":"e17f8f7c5fdafc0cffc83868e6889f94a15475c485b97c3b70ebc263ffba4457"},"suggested_fix":"Give each a plain declaration before it inside @supports, and run kit_unguarded_mixes over home.css too.","summary":"home.css's color-mix() declarations have no plain fallback or @supports guard, unlike kit.css","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:52.295848Z","id":"7f5b95b8c490128e25ebbf2e3b73160245d86797f35fff30ed48acaf90f2db6e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:448da8e65","summary":"menu-hover and menu-press tokens (dark #3a3a36, #46453f) drive .h-menu-item:hover/:active. 'a menu item's hover and press differ from the menu and each other' failed before (one colour) and passes: `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app` exit 0. The Flutter menus were not changed (their item overlay is Material's onSurface state layer, not hoverColor).","supersedes":"e7be1a689221fdfa64dba1e68365eaaee8a71cdafacf69ed517cf28540bf633e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:52.338366Z","id":"40a0da42ca7677ec6757b70b76bf408e8cc264af2105b140710a796e04e47cb5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:448da8e65","summary":"Each home.css color-mix() sits in @supports after a plain fallback, and sync-tokens.py checks home.css and map.js's stylesheet. Before the fix the check named all eight lines; cases 14 and 15 of scripts/test-sync-tokens.sh: `bazelisk test //scripts:sync_tokens //design:tokens_sync` PASSED.","supersedes":"ef32771d27ca50788a1d3d32df30bb1ff9ea0729bb46ee5297132b64cef292f4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:52.380211Z","id":"9174eb2dcc39e458d8b4a96e9f95bb501149acdd6613af35edba028fa9dc53df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:448da8e65","summary":"In dark a held or dragging face adds 0 0 0 1px var(--border-hover) to the lift shadow. 'a lifted tile carries a 1 px border-hover outline' failed before and passes: `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=home-app` exit 0.","supersedes":"e3a4062495cac85d634909c6cecf5ff66136f80ddc92de0836b7f7361d79c850","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:42:37.662089Z","id":"98d6093d60b108d62a99f50f7db827b6c5e1c2241779c98daab34884f9acbbfe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:790b8b4c2","summary":"Fixed: home.js draws every glyph from apps/clax_app/home/symbols.js (Material Symbols Rounded), icon words mapped as launcher.dart iconFor; harness test 'every glyph is a filled Material Symbol: no Lucide strokes anywhere' passes (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep --test_arg=home-app: 19 passed)","supersedes":"eababe2045111ea27f11c11f4c175c5936921613c18a35d39620e13100eabf1b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:42:37.710991Z","id":"99976309150129292ded1596e2fda1ccc6fc30ebb3b530250e63bffda2d38589","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.1 puts New app in the rail on wide Android and in File › New App and the toolbar on the Mac. Neither exists yet, so hiding the FAB at form \"wide\" now would leave no way to make an app there. The home app hides it only through chrome().toolbar, which plan Task 47 adds; the launcher needs the same once the rail (Task 53) and the Mac toolbar (Task 44) land.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2326},"end":{"line":2329},"content_hash":"061dd1de98128b7b59fce0e133fee96907e0de47cbb8f8576a610c0a608dc6c7"},"summary":"New app shows at every form, not on the phone only: on wide Android and the Mac the home app and the fallback launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart floatingActionButton) still draw the FAB","tags":["revisit:when the rail or the Mac toolbar offers New app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:54:45.735758Z","id":"af46942d2d9a30792045b889aafbb81e87726c428e4bb421fd0bdd27a715552e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"99976309150129292ded1596e2fda1ccc6fc30ebb3b530250e63bffda2d38589","summary":"38406c321: with chrome().toolbar the home app draws no FAB, and a Mac split window holds the toolbar (File › New App carries New app there). Wide Android, the iPad and the fallback launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart) still draw it: SplitShell holds the toolbar only with Mac window chrome, until a rail or toolbar offers New app.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:54:45.736009Z","id":"47edd7982743c2351a5a323c1b6bed6e560edf1c0af2241a1eb5fe8513cdda84","body":{"detail":"With chrome().toolbar the Bar (Search, Inbox, Settings, the ⋮ menu with Refresh and 'Big tiles for apps you use') is not drawn. Inbox and Settings stay in the menu bar; docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.4 says the toolbar's Search filters the sidebar and, with Home selected, the grid, but SplitShell declares no Search item, so the grid cannot be searched on the Mac. Big tiles are not drawn at form 'wide', so the switch has nothing to change there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2163},"end":{"line":2165},"content_hash":"6c3b863178e4b00620aaea988599b095c1701c9b92f1d70e7fab13160e4713b9"},"suggested_fix":"Declare the NSSearchToolbarItem and pass its text to the home app (a home event the page answers by opening its Results), and give View › Reload App the home app's refresh.","summary":"Under the Mac toolbar the home app loses its search of the grid, Refresh and the Big tiles switch: the toolbar declares no Search item yet, and only the sidebar's filter narrows anything","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:14:03.736958Z","id":"542878b05a94f568dbb9c6c2a8309327323c737d99c5ed201017fb1b22ca6956","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5af258781","summary":"Search and Refresh fixed in 5af258781 (with the toolbar search item from e05e3fb22): under a held toolbar the home app's toolbar items end with Refresh and a search field whose text reaches the page as chrome().query and filters the grid through search() and Results; View › Reload App is Refresh with Home selected. Passing: home.test.js 'with the window's toolbar, its search text (chrome's query) filters the grid…' (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='fake home capability': PASSED, 105 passed), app_screen_home_test 'on the Mac, while the window holds the toolbar for it…', home_host_test 'while the toolbar is held its search text is chrome()'s query…' and 'refresh lists the apps…', app_menu_test 'View › Reload App runs what it is given…', ToolbarTests 'testASearchItemIsASearchFieldThatSendsItsTextAsItChanges' (//apps/clax_app:macos_toolbar_test PASSED). The Big tiles switch is not given back: it is carried by the needs-decision record on apps/clax_app/home/home.js:2384.","supersedes":"47edd7982743c2351a5a323c1b6bed6e560edf1c0af2241a1eb5fe8513cdda84","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:14:04.754313Z","id":"9ac111da521e1ed19d84456c7811f5946c811869c1434d7966ac3c4637a56400","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.3 and its draft decision 9 ('Big tiles show only at phone size', which the owner may override) put big tiles on the phone only. No Settings screen has a Big tiles switch (lib/ui/settings_screen.dart's Home screen section has Open in comment mode, Undo last change, Reset and Use the built-in home screen). Options: (a) keep big tiles phone-only and the switch in the phone's ⋮ menu, as now; (b) draw big tiles at form 'wide' too and add 'Big tiles for apps you use' to Settings › Home screen, writing layout/main's bigTiles through HomeLayout (lib/home/home_layout.dart); (c) add the switch to Settings › Home screen on every platform, changing only what a phone shows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2384},"end":{"line":2384},"content_hash":"20d8118839d484fdd88ef082342ce7b84fa33a23bf8073317ffe379ba21f1740"},"summary":"Big tiles have no switch on the Mac: they are drawn at form 'phone' only and a Mac split always answers form 'wide', so the switch (the ⋮ menu's 'Big tiles for apps you use', not drawn under the toolbar) would change nothing there","tags":["status:needs-decision","home","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:14:04.755782Z","id":"d7efc964e2f7dfd42e1b05c9a4fead9711cbf35785774bb97ff066143429e31a","body":{"detail":"The toolbar's text reaches the page only as chrome().query; opening an app (home.open) needs the person's tap or key press in the page (no_gesture otherwise, web/shell/src/caps/home.ts), and a key in the native field is neither. Opening it from Dart would need the page's ranking (home/search.js) in Dart or a new host call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2371},"end":{"line":2375},"content_hash":"12a198b1c974abaccf392a68e88a1cf8c0479fb2fe0053f89e49921a83f51bcd"},"suggested_fix":"Send Return from the NSSearchField (Toolbar.swift searchChanged sees it as an action) and have AppScreen open the first app search() ranks, or add a home event the page answers by opening its first result.","summary":"Return in the toolbar's search field does not open the first match, as Enter in the page's own field does","tags":["home","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/home.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:22:19.714926Z","id":"aeb689ccb29fcb4522f74e4b6924e9706c2912e08353163781881b20e701fd87","body":{"detail":"Flutter's rows, tiles and buttons show the arrow (apps/clax_app/test/ui/hover_test.dart), and the shell's app mode already sets cursor: default on html.app.mac controls (web/shell/src/app/app.css:70). The home app gets chrome().platform == 'macos' and could do the same; it is a home bundle change with its own home_unit and home tests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"eb8e75496f8e946777e4ccb9bbe6d4aa3f0fc24a1b6890a5221c22e6cbe9039f"},"summary":"The home app's tiles, its action buttons and other controls set cursor: pointer, so on the Mac the grid in the split window's detail shows the pointing hand, where §4.10 asks for the arrow over tiles and buttons","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
